const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"先说明为什么这些价格属于同一对象",en:"Explain why the prices represent one economic object"},body:{zh:"Hasbrouck将同一证券理解得较宽，可以包含经套利关系转换后可比较的相关价格。但共同经济对象是模型前提，不是看到相关性就成立。现货、期货或不同场所报价需要先处理单位、合约与转换关系，再讨论共同价格。",en:"Hasbrouck allows economically linked prices, including transformed derivative prices, to represent one security. That shared object is a modeling premise, not a consequence of high correlation alone. Units, contracts and conversion relationships must be reconciled before imposing a common price."},reference:{url:"https://www.bauer.uh.edu/rsusmel/phd/hasbrouck95.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · pp. 1176–1177",en:"1995 journal article · pp. 1176–1177"}}},{title:{zh:"价格可以各自游走，差异却有限",en:"Prices can wander while their difference remains bounded"},body:{zh:"协整描述各价格可能非平稳，但某些价格差组合仍然平稳。论文用一个市场先变、另一个延迟反应的例子解释共同趋势与暂时偏离。共同趋势并不要求所有报价每秒一致，也不意味着每次偏离都能无成本套利。",en:"Cointegration allows individual prices to be nonstationary while a combination of their differences remains stationary. A delayed-response example separates a common trend from temporary deviations. This does not require identical quotes every second or costless arbitrage whenever prices differ."},reference:{url:"https://www.bauer.uh.edu/rsusmel/phd/hasbrouck95.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · §I",en:"1995 journal article · §I"}}},{title:{zh:"只回归收益的领先滞后可能遗漏约束",en:"Return lead-lag regressions can omit the long-run constraint"},body:{zh:"作者展示，忽略协整关系的有限滞后收益回归可能看起来系数合理，却误描绘信息传递所需时间。误差修正表示把价格偏离与短期变化放在同一个框架中。一个漂亮的领先滞后图并不足以证明某市场真正贡献了新信息。",en:"A finite-lag return regression that ignores cointegration can look well behaved while misrepresenting transmission delays. Error correction combines price discrepancies and short-run changes. An appealing lead-lag chart alone does not establish which market contributes new information."},reference:{url:"https://www.bauer.uh.edu/rsusmel/phd/hasbrouck95.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · §I · pp. 1178–1179",en:"1995 journal article · §I · pp. 1178–1179"}}},{title:{zh:"信息份额的分母是共同创新方差",en:"The denominator is common innovation variance"},body:{zh:"信息份额衡量某市场创新对共同随机游走价格创新方差的贡献比例。成交额更大、报价更多或先成交，都不直接等于这一统计量更大。它回答的是特定模型中永久价格变化的来源，而不是哪个市场整体最好或最容易交易。",en:"An information share measures a market innovation's contribution to the variance of the common random-walk innovation. Larger turnover, more quotes or earlier trades do not directly determine it. It concerns permanent price variation within a model, not overall venue quality."},reference:{url:"https://www.bauer.uh.edu/rsusmel/phd/hasbrouck95.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · §III · p. 1182",en:"1995 journal article · §III · p. 1182"}}},{title:{zh:"同时变化会使唯一分解变困难",en:"Simultaneous changes complicate unique attribution"},body:{zh:"当不同市场创新同期相关时，方差不能简单独立相加。论文通过改变Cholesky分解中的排序，为各市场计算信息份额的上界与下界。排序会影响归属，因此只挑一个顺序给出精确百分比，可能隐藏识别上的不确定性。",en:"Contemporaneously correlated innovations prevent a simple independent variance allocation. Reordering the Cholesky factorization yields upper and lower information-share bounds. Reporting one precise percentage from a chosen ordering can conceal this identification uncertainty."},reference:{url:"https://www.bauer.uh.edu/rsusmel/phd/hasbrouck95.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · §III · p. 1183",en:"1995 journal article · §III · p. 1183"}}},{title:{zh:"更细采样有帮助，但不能消除全部相关",en:"Finer sampling helps but does not eliminate correlation"},body:{zh:"较粗时间间隔可能把先后发生的报价更新合并为同一时点变化。作者因而使用很细的采样，但也明确说缩短间隔不能彻底消除同期相关。时间戳精度、市场时钟和同步方式，应与信息份额结果一起解释，不能只保留最终排名。",en:"Coarse intervals can collapse sequential quote updates into apparently simultaneous changes. The paper uses fine sampling but notes that shorter intervals do not eliminate contemporaneous correlation. Timestamp precision and synchronization belong alongside the reported shares, not behind a simple ranking."},reference:{url:"https://www.bauer.uh.edu/rsusmel/phd/hasbrouck95.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · §III · p. 1183",en:"1995 journal article · §III · p. 1183"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"信息份额分解的是共同价格创新的方差，不是成交量份额。共同趋势、采样频率和同期相关影响解释；相关创新下通常应报告界限而非唯一排名。",en:"Information shares allocate common-price innovation variance, not trading volume. Common trends, sampling and contemporaneous correlation matter; correlated innovations generally require bounds rather than a unique ranking."}};export{e as default};
